Create the Nerves rootdisk symlink for nested userdata firmware

The FP3 root filesystem is a device-mapper subpartition inside the Android
userdata partition. erlinit cannot infer the parent firmware device from that
device-mapper node, so it does not create /dev/rootdisk0 itself. Create the
standard Nerves symlink while the initramfs still has the base device path.

This lets nerves_runtime run ops.fw against /dev/mmcblk0p62 instead of an
absent (or incorrectly inferred) device.

Signed-off-by: Marc <marc@citronics.com>

--- a/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/functions.sh
+++ b/initramfs/usr/share/citronics-initramfs/functions.sh
@@ -373,6 +373,11 @@
     else
         echo_kmsg "No subpartition mapping required for $rootfs"
     fi
+
+    # The rootfs is a device-mapper node, so erlinit cannot infer its parent
+    # firmware device. Publish the conventional Nerves path before switch_root.
+    ln -sf "$base_device" /dev/rootdisk0
+    echo_kmsg "Created /dev/rootdisk0 -> $base_device"
 }
 
 mount_rootfs() {
